# Data format

The public code archive intentionally does not redistribute benchmark datasets.
To reproduce the DSD2F entries of Tables 9 and 10, place the prepared MATLAB
files in this directory using these names:

- `20NEWS.mat`    (`n=18846`, `r=20`)
- `CANCER.mat`    (`n=190`, `r=14`)
- `CITESEER.mat`  (`n=3312`, `r=6`)
- `FOOTBALL.mat`  (`n=115`, `r=12`)
- `ORL.mat`       (`n=400`, `r=40`)
- `PROTEIN.mat`   (`n=17766`, `r=3`)
- `REUTERS.mat`   (`n=8293`, `r=65`)
- `SEG.mat`       (`n=2310`, `r=7`)
- `SPAM.mat`      (`n=4601`, `r=2`)
- `UMIST.mat`     (`n=575`, `r=20`)

Each file must contain:

- `A`: the prepared nonnegative symmetric affinity matrix;
- `gnd`: the ground-truth class labels, used only after optimization to compute RI.

The Table 9/10 rerun used the cleaned R2 data preparation (for example,
20NEWS has 18,846 samples and CANCER has 190 samples). It is a separate
rerun from the historical experiment reported earlier in the manuscript.
